warning[K0841]: `===` is the same as `==` in Klass
 --> equality-warnings.kl:5:13
  |
5 |       if (x === undefined) trace('none')
  |             ^^^
  |
  = note: `==` and `!=` are always strict in Klass
help: use `==`
  |
5 |       if (x == undefined) trace('none')
  |             ~~

warning[K0840]: `undefined` is only supported for JavaScript compatibility
 --> equality-warnings.kl:5:17
  |
5 |       if (x === undefined) trace('none')
  |                 ^^^^^^^^^ use `null` instead
  |
help: compare with `null`: `x == null` matches both null and undefined
  |
5 |       if (x === null) trace('none')
  |                 ~~~~
